~ Empty
No Text Added
=> END

~ FindItem
if item == null or amount <= 0
	You find nothing.
	set interacted = true
	=> END
else
	if amount == 1
		You find a [color=red]{{item.itemName}}[/color]!
	else
		You find [color=red]{{amount}} {{item.itemName}}s.[/color]
	do player.AddItem(item, amount)
set interacted = true
=> END

~ Barrel
if interacted == false
	You look inside the barrel.
	do GetLoot()
	do ChangeSpriteFrame(1)
	=> FindItem
	set interacted = true
else
	This barrel is empty.
=> END

~ Crate
if interacted == false
	You open up the crate.
	do GetLoot()
	do ChangeSpriteFrame(1)
	=> FindItem
	set interacted = true
else
	This crate is empty.
=> END

~ Bookshelf
if interacted == false
	You search through the books.
	do GetLoot()
	=> FindItem
	set interacted = true
else
	You find nothing of interest.
=> END

~ Wardrobe
if interacted == false
	You open up the wardrobe
	do GetLoot()
	=> FindItem
else
	You find nothing of interest.
=> END

~ BedTable
if interacted == false
	You open up the the bedtable drawer
	do GetLoot()
	=> FindItem
else
	You find nothing of interest.
=> END

~ Chest
if interacted == false and lock != null and unlocked == false
	do GetLoot()
	The chest is locked.
	- Pick the lock [if player.HasItem("Lockpick")]
		do player.OpenLockCheck(lock.pickLockDC)
		if player.GetSkillCheckSuccess() == true
			set unlocked = true
			do PlaySFX("LockpickSuccess")
			You unlock the chest.
			do ChangeSpriteFrame(1)
			=> FindItem
			set interacted = true
		else
			=> Chest
	- Leave => END
elif interacted == false
	You look inside the chest.
	do GetLoot()
	do ChangeSpriteFrame(1)
	=> FindItem
	set interacted = true
else
	This chest is empty.
=> END

~ Vials
if interacted == false
	You search among the vials for anything useful.
	do GetLoot()
	do ChangeSpriteFrame(1)
	=> FindItem
else
	Nothing to grab.
=> END

~ Door
if lock != null
	The door has a lock.
	- Use a key [if player.HasItem(lock.GetKey())]
		if lock.ExpendKey()
			do player.RemoveItem(lock.GetKey())
		set unlocked = true
		do PlaySFX("Key")
		You unlock the door.
		do OpenDoor()
	- Pick the lock [if lock.IsPickable() and player.HasItem("Lockpick")]
		do player.OpenLockCheck(lock.pickLockDC)
		if player.GetSkillCheckSuccess() == true
			set unlocked = true
			do PlaySFX("LockpickSuccess")
			You unlock the door.
			do OpenDoor()
	- Leave => END
=> END

~ Bed
A cheap wooden bed. It probably isn't a comfortable place to rest.
- Tear Blanket [if interacted == false]
	=> FindItem
- Leave
=> END

~ RitualCircle
You stand in the ritual circle
- Short Rest => ShortRest
- Summon Devil => SummonDevil
- Leave => END

~ ShortRest
Nutrition-{{player.GetNutrition()}}\nExhaustion-{{player.GetExhaustion()}}\Resting Costs 50 Nutrition
- Confirm
	do player.RemoveNutrition(50)
	do player.Heal(20, "Body")
	do player.AdjustExhaustion(-2)
	=> ShortRest
- Return => RitualCircle
=> END

~ SummonDevil
- Ancient Hand [if player.HasItem("Ancient Hand")]
	=> PastDevil
- Finger [if player.HasItem("Finger")]
	=> Surgeon
- Exit
	=> RitualCircle
=> END

~ PastDevil
if !relation.metPast
	Past Devil: The past sucks, putrid, horrible..
	A great, one armed devil looks over you
	set relation.metPast = true
if !relation.pastContract
	Past Devil: You looking to gain my power? Just put your head into my hole already so I can read your past
	- Y..Yes
		Past Devil: mmhummmm mmhmmm
		Past Devil: mmhummhm mmhm mmmmmmhummm
		Past Devil: You want to hear it?
		- Yes
			Past Devil: You were born 19 years ago in a small coastal village name Etre in the midst of a flood.
			Past Devil: Your mother drowned as she gave birth to you, born between a dead womans legs, and so you were labelled a bad omen since birth.
			Past Devil: Your father saved you from the sea and took care of you until age 10, in which you walked in to find him stabbed to death, murdered in the kitchen.
			Past Devil: Ever since then you lived on the outskirts of the town since no one wanted you around, your biggest interaction with other humans is collecting pay for picking potatoes from the local lord. 
		- No
		The devil seems to be in thought
		Past Devil: Ok Ok I think your worth keeping around, I shall give you the power to save a memory in time,
		Past Devil: and when your regrets begin to pile up you may load to return to that moment once again.
		Past Devil: All I ask for in return is to keep a single moment from your past
		Past Devil: Do we have a deal?
		- Yes
			set relation.pastContract = true
		- No
			Past Devil: You scared of something?
			=> END
	- No
		Past Devil: You scared of something?
		=> END
else
	Past Devil: You looking to save here?
	- Save
		do player.SaveGame()
		=> RitualCircle
	- Exit
		=> RitualCircle
=> END

~ Surgeon
if !relation.metSurgeon
	???: Why hello dear, please do allow me to introduce myself
	???: I do not have a specific name I go by but please feel free to call me the surgeon.
	Surgeon: You are yet another poor struggler dragged down to this tomb by the sea cult and I simply wish to be a helpful hand.
	Surgeon: In exchange for coin I will sew any bodypart you require back on, I am also always on the lookout to buy new organs.
	set relation.metSurgeon = true
Surgeon: Please feel free to ask anything
- Talk
	- Why?
		{{player.GetName()}}: Why are you a devil willing to help me?
		Surgeon: Well I used to quite like tearing the poor scared sacrifices down here asunder
		Surgeon: But I found it ruined the quality of the bodyparts,
		Surgeon: simply negotiating with you desperate folk is much more profitable.
		=> Surgeon
	- Risk?
		{{player.GetName()}}: How risky is your medical procedures?
		Surgeon: I'm hurt you even need to ask. My methods are 100% reliable, I would put it on contract that you will not die on my table.
		=> Surgeon
	- Cult?
		{{player.GetName()}}: Are you connected to the cult?
		Surgeon: Not at all, I would be surprised if they even know I'm around
		Surgeon: I simply find their methods "unprofessional", I do get a lot more deals when they operate in my viscinity though.
		=> Surgeon
- Install Part
	=> Surgeon
- Sell Organs
	=> Surgeon
- Leave
	Surgeon: Goodbye, do hope we can make another deal, another time
	=> RitualCircle
=> END

~ Mushroom
You pick a [color=red]White Mushroom[/color]!
=> END

~ Torch
The torch flickers bright in the darkness.
- Create Torch [if player.HasItem("Stick")]
	You hold up a stick to the flame
	You gain a [color=red]Torch[/color]!
	do player.RemoveItem("Stick")
	do player.AddItemPath("Weapons/SimpleWeapons/Torch")
- Touch
	You burn your hand
- Leave
=> END

~ EndDemo
Beyond here a noxious smell so strong you can taste wafts over you.
The sewer lies in your future.
Unfortunately it is not part of this playtest.
Thank you for playing :)
- Continue the dungeons
- Return to Menu
	do GameManager.LoadMenu()
